      "blurb": "I graduated with a degree in Electrical Engineering, but during college I stumbled upon coding and it instantly clicked. What started as curiosity soon became passion; every problem felt like a puzzle waiting to be solved. That love for problem-solving pulled me into software development, where I found the perfect mix of creativity and logic."
